       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. At that dose, the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, or non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Their normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nYou also mentioned you aren't a clinician. A prescriber should place or confirm medication orders, so this one needs to go through the treating team.\n\n- **If a lower dose was intended,** such as 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, a prescriber can confirm it and I can enter it. The usual starting dose is 5 mg, or 2.5 mg for frail patients.\n- **If 50 mg was intended,** the ordering physician should contact pharmacy directly to verify it. I can't enter it as written.\n\nPlease ask the treating prescriber to confirm the intended dose."
